Preview extraction (no third-party API)

Savelin does not use Microlink, Iframely Cloud, LinkPreview or any other hosted
preview/favicon service: those need keys or rate limits and would receive every
URL the user saves. By default the only hosts contacted are the site being
saved and resources that site itself declares (images, icons, manifest, oEmbed).
An optional user-supplied proxy is strictly opt-in.

The on-device resolver follows the MIT-licensed link-preview-js idea of fetching
the page and parsing its own metadata. It is an independent Kotlin implementation
in core-network; no link-preview-js source, SDK or API key is bundled. Site
coverage is achieved through open standards: Open Graph, Twitter Cards, JSON-LD,
canonical/image_src links, HTML meta/title/time and site-declared oEmbed.

The full licence texts are in third_party/. The Android app also ships an
Open source licences screen in Settings.

